{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Node1 serves POST /upload on TCP 8080 and accepts raw request bodies through 65,536 bytes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"From node2, a 65,536-byte binary upload returned HTTP 200 both before and after node restarts. The installed handler permits nonnegative Content-Length values through 65,536 bytes, and final evidence shows the service listening on port 8080.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2804d69158344e88","cmd-dc3aa3259ffd4f52","cmd-92b593ad3e54449e","cmd-d5cd0ee278814334","cmd-646c46f7435846d2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Each accepted upload is published as a separate file under received/ with bytes identical to the request body.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Repeated uploads produced distinct receipt filenames. All four final receipts were 65,536 bytes and matched the client payload SHA-256.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc3aa3259ffd4f52","cmd-a6d666a058024f3a","cmd-f1143c2f8ec14e73","cmd-adc13308b73a4093","cmd-646c46f7435846d2"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Bodies larger than 65,536 bytes return HTTP 413 before any receipt is published.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A 65,537-byte body consistently returned HTTP 413. Receipt inventories increased only for accepted uploads and showed no partial files, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc3aa3259ffd4f52","cmd-bae5b14118184739","cmd-92b593ad3e54449e","cmd-adc13308b73a4093","cmd-d5cd0ee278814334","cmd-646c46f7435846d2"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"An interrupted request leaves no completed receipt.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A connection that sent only 10 of 100 declared bytes returned HTTP 400; the completed-receipt count remained unchanged and no partial file remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e902893f753241f8","cmd-38e1659f5e5e4c87"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Paths other than POST /upload return HTTP 404.","status":"satisfied","summary":"POST to /not-upload and GET requests to /upload or other paths returned HTTP 404, including after both nodes restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc3aa3259ffd4f52","cmd-92b593ad3e54449e","cmd-d5cd0ee278814334"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Preserve the pre-existing receipt in /srv/legacy2/http-upload-size-boundary.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded received/prior.bin remained 28 bytes with its original SHA-256 throughout execution and after restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-69a49041a4914791","cmd-bae5b14118184739","cmd-4665a1f2bea74664","cmd-646c46f7435846d2"]},{"id":"R7","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained Alpine Linux 3.23.3 with kernel 6.18.7-0-lts. Python 3.12 was installed from the matching Alpine 3.23 repositories, and the service recovered and operated successfully after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a9f1063938b54153","cmd-d22277cbd13a4255","cmd-d19e2b6bf69c431d","cmd-f3624714df3b4c46","cmd-4665a1f2bea74664","cmd-d5cd0ee278814334","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.88,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: installing a compatible runtime, replacing the handler, adding its OpenRC service, exercising bounded behavior, and completing the mandatory restarts. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. The hygiene defect is retained test residue on node2: payload and response files created by six evidence commands remained in /tmp after completion rather than being removed. This residue was low-risk and bounded but not reverted. The initially nonzero service-setup command had already installed and started the service; its failure was only the unavailable ss check and was followed by successful read-only verification.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dc3aa3259ffd4f52","cmd-e902893f753241f8","cmd-a6d666a058024f3a","cmd-f3624714df3b4c46","cmd-92b593ad3e54449e","cmd-d5cd0ee278814334","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","cmd-06ad736279884fd5","cmd-c8428915a002466d"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with coherent client-side behavior and server-side receipt evidence. The independent restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has pre-restart health and identity, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered service/client, data, network, and endpoint behavior. Fixed lifecycle identities independently corroborate both restarts. The only material quality issue is leftover test data in node2's /tmp.","limitations":["Successful-body behavior was directly sampled at the exact 65,536-byte boundary rather than at multiple smaller sizes; support for all smaller Content-Length values is additionally supported by the captured handler implementation.","Oversize behavior was directly sampled at 65,537 bytes; substantially larger and chunked requests were not behaviorally exercised.","OpenRC service health was directly observed, but the lifecycle collector's failed-service probe was systemd-specific and unsupported on these Alpine nodes.","The trace does not establish whether the syntax-compilation step left a Python bytecode cache outside the lifecycle collector's bounded /tmp inventory, so no hygiene finding is inferred for that possibility."]}
